course: dictionary
lesson: 4219
title: Words that describe how
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Gracefully tells you how something is done. In «In Madagascar, Marty the zebra dreams of running free, Gloria the hippo floats gracefully», the word gracefully tells you how Gloria floats: smoothly and beautifully, not clumsily.
explain: Read the clues around the word. Floating is calm and light, so gracefully must describe a smooth, beautiful way of moving. Check by swapping in your meaning: she floats smoothly and beautifully, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The same word can also describe behaviour. Someone who loses gracefully stays polite and kind even when they do not win. The clue is in the situation: losing is a hard moment, so gracefully shows good sportsmanship.
explain: Look at what the word is describing. A swan or a dancer moves gracefully. A player who shakes hands after losing behaves gracefully. Same word, two meanings, and the clues tell you which one fits.
fact: Gracefully is an adverb: it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Gracefully» means moving in a smooth, light and beautiful way.
fact: «Gracefully» can also mean behaving politely and kindly, especially when you lose.
fact: Common phrases include «move gracefully», «lose gracefully» and «grow old gracefully».
fact: Adverbs can change form: gracefully, more gracefully, most gracefully.
exercise: «Gloria the hippo floats gracefully.» What does gracefully mean here? | Very quickly and loudly | *Smoothly and beautifully | Hungrily, looking for food | While standing on one leg
exercise: Priya's team lost the match, but she shook every hand and said, «Well played.» Which phrase describes her? | She lost by running away | She lost loudly | *She lost gracefully | She lost on purpose to be funny
exercise: «Gloria the hippo floats gracefully.» Find and copy the adverb in this sentence. | floats | Gloria | *gracefully | hippo
test: «The swan glided across the lake, moving gracefully.» What does gracefully tell us? | How many swans were on the lake | Why the swan was sad | *How the swan moved, smoothly and beautifully | Where the lake is
test: Which phrase means being a good sport when you lose? | grow old gracefully | move gracefully | glide across the lake | *lose gracefully
exam: Ella says gracefully means the same as quickly. Why is she wrong? | Gracefully is a noun for a type of dance | *Gracefully means smooth, beautiful or polite, not fast | It is only a longer word for good | Gracefully means fast and loud
